//! The AArch64 SIMD, floating-point and SVE encoding table, and the
//! general-purpose groups that are families of the same kind: the load/store
//! exclusives, the acquire/release accesses, the atomics, pointer
//! authentication and memory tagging.
//!
//! Generated by `tools/tables/aarch64.py` from llvm-mc; do not edit. Each
//! row is one instruction form: a mnemonic, the operands it takes, the
//! opcode left when every operand is zero, and which instruction-set
//! features the target needs for it. The generator measured each field by
//! assembling the form with one operand changed at a time, and checked every
//! row against llvm-mc before writing it here; the feature set is the one
//! GNU as's own opcode table gives the row this form encodes.
//!
//! 6794 forms, 1365 operand shapes, 426 distinct operands.
